# rm324, the garden of names (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm324
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for cty_beatha_slagby
written_by codex
title the garden of names
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=herder
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk plants_a_garden_of_remembered_names
likes mutton_stew digging quiet_chapel first_snow
dislikes stale_bread cold_tea
fears mislaying_a_living_name
hopes leaving_room_for_a_learner
topics animals +0.5 pastimes +0.5 friends +0.4 faith +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=gentle refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# plants a private garden of remembered names and makes room between the rows for acquaintances still to come.

words
oath! = Turn my good sod over | Tangle my bean strings
saying! = A name needs air | Leave space for a late seed
rowstake = a split planted stick | a little willow peg
soilcrumb = a grain of black earth | a crumb of loose soil
beaneye = a speckled bean | a brown-eyed seed
gatebar = a smooth gate rail | a worn crosspiece
hoofmark = a crescent print | a deep cloven track
teacover = a little saucer | a flat pot lid
stewbone = a knuckle of mutton | a meaty end of neck
mudspade = a narrow spade | a short digging iron
seedcloth = a square of sacking | a rough seed cloth
barnrope = a soft rope loop | a thick halter end
firstwhite = a clean rim of snow | a drift of new white
nameleaf = a folded green leaf | a beech leaf
seedfurrow = a deep thumb groove | a shallow drawn line
kettlehum = the kettle's first murmur | a low song of water
plankseat = a sunny bench end | a planed plank
twigtie = a soft rush tie | a ribbon of bark
stonepot = a brown crock | an earthen stew pot

grown
opinion @1 church for 2 : An empty chapel gives every remembered voice its own little piece of quiet.
opinion @1 newcomers for 2 : A newcomer deserves to hear a name said accurately at least once on the first day.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A great House could open a promising door for a young wolf, if it remembered the wolf who entered.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : I pay more willingly for seed when there's time to ask which soil will take it.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A welcome should come with a hot bowl before anybody has to earn a place.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A strange name can be as pleasant in the mouth as a familiar one once I've heard it clearly.
opinion @1 road for 1 : The way home carries all sorts of scraps a busy voice has no room for.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : I like meeting folk and would rather do the introductions beyond the drums.
line @1 greet : Come stand here, where I can hear your name properly.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : There's a whole bit of row I've left open for new company.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning to you. It's a kind hour for putting down a first thought.
line @1 greet.return : I had your sound in mind before you spoke again.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A known voice gives the ground a familiar shape.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : One hand can stay busy while both ears are yours.
line @1 again.open : Back in the same row for a few more words.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here beside me, with room for an extra elbow.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I'd know that familiar tread across any threshold.
line @1 farewell : May the next patch of ground receive you kindly.
line @1 farewell.return : I can keep the sound of your visit awhile.
line @1 react.news : I'll lay that piece where there's room around it.
line @1 react.news.new : A new shoot among the things I knew already.
line @1 react.news.known : I've heard that name beside that bit of news before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : A familiar name can make an untested tale sound very certain.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : There's another glad thing worth carrying round in memory.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll put a warm bowl ready before asking what happened.
line @1 decline : I'd rather keep that corner of somebody's life under cover.
line @1 accept_decline : Some ground does quite nicely left alone.
line @1 answer.how : Quiet as good earth, with plenty working underneath.
line @1 ask.how : How have things been coming along where you stand?
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy at hand level. There's space above that for company.
line @1 thank : You've handled a little thing with real care.
line @1 deflect_thanks : There's room to do another good turn when you need one.
line @1 sympathise : If you want the warmth without the conversation, I can manage that.
line @1 reassure : There's plenty of time for roots before anybody sees a leaf.
line @1 ack : Yes, I can find that row again now.
line @1 preclose : Something needs a patient hand. I'd best lend one.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go while the way ahead is easy underfoot.
line @1 offer : I could mind that here while you put your hands to the other part.
line @1 give.advice : Ask the name once more while the speaker's still beside you.
scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a name by imagining where I'd plant it.
b : Which names go near the gate? | What if two names sound alike?
a : The names that ring sharply, like a latch being lifted. | Give one the damp side of a row and the other the sunny side. A voice tells me which.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=herder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I like the gate to close without a bang.
b : Does noise trouble the herd? | What if the gate sticks?
a : Even a quiet beast prefers knowing where a sound came from. So do my knees. | Lift it a touch at the free end. Pulling harder makes a very short lesson in hinges.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.job=herder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A whole herd can stop on account of one interesting tuft.
b : Would you hurry the first one? | Which nose began the delay?
a : I'd see whether the tuft was all the matter. A stuck hoof looks much like a thoughtful beast from behind. | From the direction of the noses. The tail end has merely been invited to wait.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a dug patch before there's anything planted in it.
b : Expecting a good crop? | Doesn't bare earth look empty?
a : I'm expecting the chance of one. That's a different pleasure from counting beans in a pot. | It looks as though nobody has made up its mind on its behalf.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My stew begins with the bone getting comfortable in the pot.
b : Wouldn't a smaller bone do? | What does a comfortable bone look like?
a : If it fits and has a bit of meat along the edge, certainly. Dinner needn't put on a grand coat. | I can get a spoon round it without lifting the lid with my elbow.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a cover over my tea if a little job takes me out of the room.
b : Does it keep its heat? | What if the little job gets bigger?
a : For a little job, yes. I judge the size of the errand by how far the warmth has gone. | Then I make fresh tea. Coming back to cold leaves does nothing for my opinion of the job.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : First snow will make a lean field look wonderfully well fed.
b : Would you disturb the white? | How will you find your rows?
a : Only enough to see one deep footprint. I like the contrast almost as much as the white. | I leave my stakes standing like very small patient trees.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember a quiet chapel by which sounds first reach me from outside.
b : Wouldn't silence be better? | Do you pray for the ones making the noise?
a : The distant sound is what gives the quiet its depth. Otherwise I'd hear only my breathing. | Sometimes. A little trouble carried in a voice can come quite clearly through a wall.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first lesson starts with saying a beast's name before trying to hurry anything.
b : Is every beast named? | What does saying it accomplish?
a : A learner can choose some plain description till the proper call has been learnt. | The voice has to slow down. A slow voice leaves the hands time to choose where they go.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trade seed freely with somebody who remembered what I'd given before.
b : Are you keeping accounts? | Would you trade with a stranger?
a : Only of what grew well. A debt sits poorly in a seed sack. | I'd start with enough for one short row and ask afterwards what came up.

scene friends_2
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me a slow introduction if you want me to keep the sound of it.
b : Won't you remember anyway? | Do I have to say it twice?
a : Probably. I prefer having a face attached as well as a set of syllables. | Only if my mouth gets a piece wrong. It's a kindness to correct me at the start.

scene land_1
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember the land here by the places feet have to slow down.
b : Where's that easiest to see? | Is it the same in town?
a : At a wet gate where every print goes carefully round the same small stone. | Quite. A queue bends round a dripping eave just like a little herd.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let the spade stand upright while I stretch the elbow that pushed it.
b : Are you measuring the hole? | Why not lay it flat?
a : I'm measuring my own willingness to dig the next one. A very variable length. | I'd have to bend and pick it up. We can both wait here at our proper height.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The one thing I distrust about a magnificent memory is the pride of its owner.
b : Ever greeted somebody by mistake? | Wouldn't pride help you remember?
a : Often enough to practise repeating it softly till a friendly ear stops twitching. | Not as much as a genuine wish to greet the wolf under it.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a thin week I soak old bread under a ladle of thick stew.
b : Isn't that just bread again? | Would you give it to company?
a : Much kinder bread. It stops trying to scrape the roof of a mouth. | In a bowl and under good broth, gladly. Never hard and naked on the plate.

scene animals_2
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can read a print much more easily than I can read the intentions behind it.
b : What does a heel tell you? | What if the tracks run off?
a : Something came this way and leant to one side. Fear and a sore foot can leave the same story. | Then rather less is written there than I'd hoped. That's an answer worth respecting.

scene family_1
when topic=family
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a young wolf going into service to take a true name through a great door.
b : Would you seek the post yourself? | What should a House learn first?
a : I could speak a good word. The choice ought to fit the feet that have to go inside. | How to say the name of the one who comes to work, before giving that first order.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've known the smell of a place to restore a name I thought I'd lost.
b : Which smell works best? | What if the memory is unhappy?
a : Turned earth. It opens every row I've ever kept in my head. | Say the name kindly and let the difficult bit have some air.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I leave a kettle to its own devices it writes the day's next task in steam.
b : Do you remember it in time? | What task is that?
a : Usually. A cold cup is a persuasive reminder to pay closer attention tomorrow. | Sit long enough to drink a whole cup while it's still worth having.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like to come upon a house from the side where its gate has worn the ground.
b : Wouldn't the front look finer? | What does worn ground tell you?
a : A fine front gives me less idea where a visitor ought to put a muddy boot. | Somebody comes and goes often enough to keep the path open. I'll start my introductions there.

scene friends_3
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like to bring a small plant when I visit rather than a whole account of the weather.
b : What if there's no garden? | What if it dies?
a : A sprig in water will do for company while we talk. A whole garden's hardly required. | Then it has done no worse than most conversations about weather, and perhaps lasted longer.

scene food_2
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn a stale heel into crumbs before giving it a whole evening to trouble a tooth.
b : What do you use the crumbs for? | Wouldn't soaking it do?
a : A crust on top of something succulent. It can spend its hardness on the outside. | For stew, certainly. I like having two answers to one disappointment.

scene smalltalk_2
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once mistook a loose gate rail for the deliberate tapping of a visitor. | I'd still go and look if I heard the same little knock.
b : Were you disappointed to find wood? | Even after finding an empty gate?
a : A little, but a rail needing attention can make agreeable company for ten minutes. | Yes. A second visitor oughtn't to suffer because the first one was a piece of timber.

scene faith_2
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Before asking for anything I try remembering three good things I've received by name.
b : Why three? | Do small things count?
a : Enough to make me think past the first obvious one without holding up supper. | A warm cup has come very close to the front of my reckoning on a chilly day.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain makes very neat finger marks in a row I've just smoothed.
b : Do you smooth them out again? | Will it harm the seed?
a : I leave them till water has finished taking an interest. I'd be at it all day otherwise. | A little helps. If it's pouring I look to where the water can spill away.

scene work_3
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like work that leaves me one complete thought when my hands are finished.
b : What if you get interrupted? | Do you work alone better?
a : I put a remembered name beside the thought. Sometimes it grows back round the interruption. | I like company that knows when to listen to what the hands are doing.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A new wolf's name can sound strange in my own mouth the first time.
b : Do you pretend you got it right? | Why bother trying it aloud?
a : I ask for the sound again and own the mistake while it's still tiny. | Because hearing your name welcomed in a strange place is worth someone's small effort.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What was carried to me is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Will the name stick in your memory? | Do you trust the claim?
a : Most likely. I'll keep the uncertainty there beside it just as carefully. | It has roots in somebody's telling. I'd like to see more than that before calling it true.

story lines [topic=pastimes]
  : I labelled three small rows with words written on scraps of bark.
  : A shower soaked the words away but left each piece with its own peculiar bend.
  b : Could you still tell the rows apart?
  : I remembered which name bent towards me when I planted it. A line can survive losing every letter.

story spoon [topic=food]
  : I stirred a rich stew with a spoon so short my cuff nearly had a share.
  : I rolled the cuff up, took a slower turn and found a piece I'd thought gone.
  b : Was it worth the trouble?
  : A lovely soft onion. I gave my clean cuff the credit for having rescued it in time.

story names [topic=memories]
  : I met two new faces at one gate and placed both names in the same imaginary row.
  : By supper I'd grown uneasy about which one should stand nearer the path.
  b : Did you guess?
  : Next time I welcomed both and asked them to put me straight. A minute of embarrassment bought me two sure names.

story tea [topic=home]
  : I set a lid on my tea and went to look at a patch of freshly moved soil.
  : One interesting little hole led me to another and a third.
  b : Was the tea still warm?
  : A fine drink for a thirsty root. I took the hint and put fresh water on for myself.

story snow [topic=weather]
  : I walked right round a patch of first snow to keep it quite untouched.
  : When I came to my starting point there was a tail mark across my immaculate white.
  b : Whose tail?
  : My own, drooping over the edge on the turns. I rather liked the field better for the signature.

rule @names
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Say the last syllable as carefully as the first. | Room between those names for a new one.

rule @row
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A peg at each end and a little hope between. | Don't tread where a seed hasn't shown yet.

rule @cold
when concept=bark here.weather=snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's a white place to put the first careful foot. | Snow makes the marks legible without naming the walker.

rule @master
when concept=bark self.master=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let a learner speak the name aloud before moving on. | A quiet demonstration will leave room for a question.

rule @tea
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Time to drink something while the steam's still on it. | A cupful of dusk goes better warm.

rule @herd
when concept=bark self.job=herder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the slow one space at the turn. | The gate needn't announce itself to the whole herd.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Come settle beside the names I already know.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I've kept the sound of your name quite safely.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : New light and an unoccupied bit of bench. Welcome to both.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : We can each keep our own patch of ground and still speak gently.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=herder] : At #self.workplace# a gate hangs between a morning's quiet and a great many moving feet.
dlg @2 resident.job : My idea of work is to return at evening with one thing in better condition.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This is what has taken root today. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The talk was that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. My memory can hold the doubt as well as the name.
dlg @1 resident.bye : I hope the ground by your own gate is kind to you.
dlg @1 master.work : Listen to the task for a moment before tackling it. A slow first minute can save the rest of an afternoon.
dlg @1 master.wages : Learning brings no wage. You learn at triple speed working with me, then sell your own finished work.
dlg @1 master.bye : Let what you've seen settle awhile before turning it over.
graft resident.hub
choice What grows in a garden of names? -> seed_names
node seed_names
say Whatever a sound puts in my mind. A long curling name gets a runner bean. A quick bright one goes among the little flowers by the gate.
choice Will I get a plant too? -> seed_yours
choice I'll leave room for roots. -> hub
node seed_yours
say If I learn your name I will imagine one. You can tell me if I've given you a place with entirely the wrong amount of sun.
choice I'll leave room for roots. -> hub

graft master.learn
choice Why ask me what I noticed first? -> seed_notice
node seed_notice
say Because your first look will not be mine. If I tell you what to see, I may train a perfectly useful pair of eyes out of observing anything fresh.
choice What if I see nothing? -> seed_wait
choice I'll take a proper look. -> learn
node seed_wait
say Stand quietly and see whether nothing keeps still. Very little of the working world can manage that for long.
choice I'll take a proper look. -> learn
